Adversarial review (independent agent, own script) of commits 2c1a1bd855 and
31023cc2f3. Every corpus number reproduced except the ones below. All
corrections are appended in the note's sections 10 and 10b, dated; first-draft
values stay visible.

HIGH, and the lead: the census carried the defect it measures. It named the
169 dict-shaped `inference_substrate` declarations and dropped them from every
aggregate but `shapes`, while the gate's `_inference_substrate_text` stringifies
them and judges them: 70 floored at 60 s by marker, 20 deterministic_verifier,
13 aggregation, 66 no floor (13 blocked, 53 ignored). A recogniser narrower than
its concept, inside the instrument built to find them. Fixed: `census_artifact`
classifies through the gate; `gate_view` (P-declared, 3108) and
`dict_shaped_gate_view` (169) sit next to the P-string aggregates, each
population named. Eighth test; mutation M7 (gate view replaced by the string
view) RED, restored byte-identically, GREEN.

Fail-open corner, two consistent definitions, never spliced: A (blocked runs
excluded, the note's definition) 60 / 16 / 76 over P-string / P-dict /
P-declared; B (blocked included) 87 / 18 / 105. The 78 that circulated during
review was 60 from A plus 18 from B. The reviewer found that itself when
challenged. Third same-day occurrence of population mixing (instrument, note,
review); recorded as such.

HIGH: one table mixed P-declared artifact counts with P-string distinct counts
in a single row. Now one column per population.

Count and wording corrections, conclusions unchanged: 24 not 25 starred
entries; five non-canonical names used >=10 times (named), not nine; seven prose
entries, not six; 123 dict key-sets, not 101; suffix rule 13.0% of recognised
artifacts / 63.3% of recognised distinct leading tokens, not "a quarter";
"the 16 strings are exact" is 14 of 16 (the two are blocked runs, named);
section 5.1 said 39 blocked where 5.2 said 251 (251, by verdict); "80 web
artifacts" now names its population; NO_LLM_SUBSTRATE_ALIASES has 76 elements
and 75 distinct (`cached_sota_event_energy_calibration` twice).

Boundary correction, headline larger: `--since=2026-08-23` resolved to a time of
day about thirteen hours after the lint's commit a76b5f03f8
(2026-08-22T23:52:52-04:00). From that commit: 41 commits touched the gate, 30
added an alias, 29 conductor, 1 outer-loop; NO_LLM 48 -> 75. The guard governed
1 of 30 widenings.

Precision: no evidence file under results/ was written or changed. An access
symlink at results/arc_leaderboard_eval_runs let a hook run; it is NOT ignored
in the worktree (trailing-slash rule matches directories only), was never
staged, and is removed after this commit.

Recommendation unchanged in substance (option B), sharpened: the class field
must be a bare string, the gate must stop stringifying dict-shaped declarations
(SUBSTRATE_DECLARATION_MALFORMED draft), and the frozen tuples get one
de-duplication in the open.

